17:T7a8,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How to file a criminal case or defense petition in Roorkee Court? (रूड़की कोर्ट में केस कैसे फाइल करें?)","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Criminal proceedings are initiated by lodging an FIR at the concerned police station or by filing a private criminal complaint under Section 200 CrPC / BNSS directly before the Judicial Magistrate Court at New Civil Court, Ramnagar, Roorkee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the procedure for obtaining anticipatory bail prior to arrest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If there is a reasonable apprehension of arrest in a non-bailable offence, an anticipatory bail petition under Section 438 CrPC / Sec 482 BNSS is filed before the Sessions Court at Haridwar or the High Court of Uttarakhand at Nainital."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to get a regular bail in a criminal case?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In general criminal matters, regular bail applications before the Magistrate or Sessions Court in Roorkee and Haridwar are typically heard within 3 to 7 working days depending on court schedules and police diary reports."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a false FIR lodged against an individual be cancelled or quashed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if an FIR is registered with malicious intent or false accusations, a petition under Section 482 CrPC can be filed before the High Court of Uttarakhand to quash the FIR and prevent unlawful police harassment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What documents are required to prepare a bail application?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Key documents include a copy of the FIR, arrest memo, identity proof of sureties, property papers for bail bonds, and relevant evidence establishing innocence or non-involvement."}}]}f:["$","div",null,{"className":"page-animate","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"appl